  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "tropica",
      "sourceUrl": "https://tropica.com/en/plants/plantdetails/Bacopamonnieri'Compact'(044ACLP)/30569",
      "html": "<ul><li>Origin: cultivar</li><li>Height: 3 - 10+ cm (average height after two months in the tank)</li><li>Light demand: low</li><li>CO2: low</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "tropica",
      "sourceUrl": "https://tropica.com/en/plants/plantdetails/Bacopamonnieri'Compact'(044ACLP)/30569",
      "html": "<p>By pinching off all vertically growing shoots, the plant can maintain a low and close growth, since it willingly creates a large number of side shoots. Furthermore, the plant grows well in the shadow of other plants. The plant becomes more vertical growing and less compact without CO2 additive and decreased light conditions.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "tropica",
      "sourceUrl": "https://tropica.com/en/plants/plantdetails/Bacopamonnieri'Compact'(044ACLP)/30569",
      "html": "<p>This culture form of the stalk plant Bacopa monnieri is more compact and, under good light conditions, almost a creeping plant. Very suitable as a somewhat higher carpet or bushy plant in the middle or front of the aquarium.</p>"
    }
  ],
